PART 5 : Stage 0: Getting to know the provided skeleton


5.2- Digging into the code

Files that will have to be changed / modified throughout the lab : 

	• Makefile.config : main settings for the runtime

	• tasks_types.h : data types and data structures for the management of tasks and their state.

	• tasks.* : implementation of the main functions of the runtime API

	• tasks_implem.* : runtime engine in charge executing the tasks (thread pool, etc.)

	• tasks_queue.* : instantiation of and operations on task queues





- Use conditional variables to wait until the common buffer is not empty.

– Acquire a lock in order to access the CS, which is, at the moment, the common task buffer.

– Dequeue the buffer and get the task to execute.

– Send a "broadcast" to tell all concerned threads that the buffer has one less element now.

– Execute the task.

